        # and the program SIGILLs long before it ever reaches the x86
        # bytes. Pad with zeros so downstream emit stays aligned. The x86
        # backend is variable-length and doesn't care about alignment, so
        # this costs nothing there — on aarch64 `_AARCH64_BACKEND == 1`.
        # v6.4.58: cx bytecode is ALSO strictly 4-byte instructions (cxvm computes
        # call/jump targets as off*4), so a raw asm block whose length isn't a
        # multiple of 4 misaligns every following fn — same class as the v6.4.54
        # DCE-stub bug. Pad on cx too. x86 is variable-length (both operands 0 →
        # no padding, byte-identical). See issue 2026-07-11-cx-naked-asm-4byte-realign.
